I have a Go service that leaks memory over days. I profiled it with pprof and the goroutine count grows unbounded. The suspect function fans out HTTP requests to multiple backends:

```go
func FetchAll(ctx context.Context, urls []string) []Result {
    ch := make(chan Result)
    for _, url := range urls {
        go func(u string) {
            resp, err := http.Get(u)
            if err != nil {
                ch <- Result{Err: err}
                return
            }
            defer resp.Body.Close()
            body, _ := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)
            ch <- Result{Data: body}
        }(url)
    }

    var results []Result
    for range urls {
        results = append(results, <-ch)
    }
    return results
}
```

Looks correct to me. Every goroutine sends exactly once, the loop reads exactly len(urls) times. Where is the leak?

